@startuml SQ-08
title SQ-08 Disconnect, reconnect & server failure [P mechanism — rules TBD OQ-GP-05]
participant "Competitor Client" as C
participant "Match Server" as MS
participant "Backend API" as B
== Disconnect ==
C -x MS : connection lost (ENet timeout or app closed)
MS -> MS : peer slot -> DISCONNECTED, start grace timer\n(P: 15 s; top behaviour during grace TBD)
MS -> B : MatchStateChanged {participantDisconnected userId}
== Reconnect within grace ==
C -> B : GET /v1/me/active-match
B --> C : {matchId, status: IN_PROGRESS}
C -> B : POST /v1/matches/{matchId}/tickets {role: COMPETITOR}
B -> B : verify user is participant of active match
B -> MS : TicketGrant {hash, userId, COMPETITOR, exp}
B --> C : {host, udpPort, ticket}
C -> MS : connect + C2S_Hello {ticket}
MS -> MS : rebind userId to new peer; cancel grace timer
MS --> C : S2C_Welcome {role, phase} + full snapshot
== Grace expired ==
MS -> MS : apply disconnect rule [TBD]: e.g. eliminate\nreason DISCONNECT, or keep top simulated
== Match Server failure ==
MS -x B : control WS closed AND no re-register\nwithin 30 s (heartbeat 5 s) [P]
B -> B : match status=ABORTED (BR-013: no competitive effect)
note right of B
  A Backend restart is NOT a match failure:
  Match Servers reconnect and re-register
  with {state: BUSY, matchId}; Backend reconciles.
  If a result later arrives for a match aborted
  only due to lost contact, it is accepted (P).
end note
B -> C : event match.aborted {matchId}
note over B : Supervisor (systemd) restarts the process;\nit re-registers as IDLE.
@enduml
